@document
  title: LDOC Structure Test Document
  short_title: Structure Test
  author: Test Suite
  numbering: decimal
  page_size: letter
  orientation: portrait
  margins:
    top: 1in
    right: 1.25in
    bottom: 1in
    left: 1.25in
  spacing:
    line: 1.15
    before: 6pt
    after: 6pt
  styles:
    body:
      font: Times New Roman
      size: 12pt
    heading1:
      font: Arial
      size: 16pt
      bold: true
    heading2:
      font: Arial
      size: 14pt
      bold: true

// =============================================================================
// LDOC Structure Test Corpus
// =============================================================================
// This file covers all structure-related LDOC features for parser verification.
// Each section demonstrates a specific feature with comments explaining usage.
//
// The @document block above defines document-level settings.
// All settings are optional. Keys use snake_case or dash-case.
// Supported settings:
//   - title, short_title, author
//   - numbering: default or decimal
//   - page_size: letter or a4
//   - orientation: portrait or landscape
//   - margins: nested object with top/right/bottom/left
//   - spacing: line multiplier and before/after paragraph spacing
//   - styles: nested for body, heading1, heading2, etc.

// =============================================================================
// @import Directive
// =============================================================================
// Import other LDOC files to include their definitions and content.
// Paths are relative to the current file.
// Note: Importing a non-existent file will error at compile time.
// Example (commented out to avoid error):
// @import(./shared-definitions.ldoc)

// =============================================================================
// @meta Block
// =============================================================================
// Metadata block for document-specific data accessible via variables.
// Supports simple key-value pairs, nested objects, and arrays.

@meta
  version: 1.0
  status: draft
  keywords: structure, test, corpus
  contact:
    name: Test Author
    email: test@example.com
  reviewers: Alice, Bob, Carol
@end

// =============================================================================
// Headers (Multiple Levels)
// =============================================================================
// Markdown-style headers from H1 through H6.

# Heading Level 1

## Heading Level 2

### Heading Level 3

#### Heading Level 4

##### Heading Level 5

###### Heading Level 6

// =============================================================================
// @anchor Directive
// =============================================================================
// Create a named anchor for cross-references within the document.

@anchor(section-introduction)

This paragraph follows the anchor and can be referenced using [[section-introduction]].

@anchor("Section 5.2")

Anchors can have quoted names with special characters.

// =============================================================================
// Page and Column Layout
// =============================================================================

// @pagebreak - Forces a new page
@pagebreak

## Page Layout Section

This content appears on a new page after the page break.

// @columns - Multi-column layout with options
// Syntax: @columns(count, gap: length, separator)

@columns(2, gap: 0.5in)
  ### Two Column Layout
  
  This is the left column content. Text flows naturally between columns.
  
  @break
  
  This text appears in the right column after the column break.
@end

@columns(3, gap: 0.25in, separator)
  Column one content.
  
  @break
  
  Column two content.
  
  @break
  
  Column three content with a separator line between columns.
@end

// =============================================================================
// @header and @footer Directives
// =============================================================================
// Document headers and footers with page-specific variants.

// Default header (appears on all pages unless overridden)
@header
  Document Title - Page {page} of {pages}
@end

// Default footer
@footer
  Confidential - {date}
@end

// First page header (different header for the first page)
@firstpage @header
  Welcome to the Document
@end

// First page footer
@firstpage @footer
  First Page Footer
@end

// Even page header (for double-sided printing)
@evenpage @header
  Even Page Header - {short_title}
@end

// Even page footer
@evenpage @footer
  Even Page Footer
@end

// =============================================================================
// Single-line Header/Footer Variants
// =============================================================================
// Headers and footers can also be single-line:

@header Single-line header content

@footer Single-line footer content

// =============================================================================
// Additional Structure Examples
// =============================================================================

## Mixed Content Section

This section demonstrates that structure directives can be mixed with
regular content paragraphs and other elements.

@center This paragraph is centered.

@bold This paragraph is bold.

@indent:2 This paragraph is double-indented.

### Nested Headers Work

Content continues after nested headers.

// =============================================================================
// End of Structure Test Corpus
// =============================================================================
